> An idea would be to adapt the F1 system:
> 
> For each class, give the team 10pts if one of their members is 1st,
> 8pts if a team member is 2nd, 6pts if a member is 3rd, 5pts if a
> member is 4th, and so on.

This sounds like a good, simple system. To be clear, one person
could not score for both first and second place, right?

It encourages teams to coordinate and watch what other teams are
doing, it prevents members from having negative contribution, it
rules out people trying to hack a weighting formula in boring
ways (where Team Play Only Valkyries is declared a winner after
Team Have Script That Starts A Billion Games and Does '<yq' On First
Turn is controversially disqualified). It provides a limit to how
much any one game can contribute to the total--you might be
wasting your time killing Death over and over. It limits how much
any one player can contribute meaning you probably need a team.

